# network-o11y-demo — agent context

- **Paths:** `terraform/colocated-network-lab/` (EC2 fabric + k3s, `make -C local colocated-lab-up`) | `local/` (laptop: Docker + ContainerLab + Compose) | legacy `terraform/` + `k8s/telemetry/` (EKS blog). **Destination is Alloy** (SNMP/traps/syslog/flow addons) replacing KtransToGrafana; laptop `make up` still defaults to ktranslate — `docs/ktranslate-unified-model.md` / `docs/alloy-network-fork.md`. **Until the operator says otherwise, work on AWS colocated** (do not bring the laptop Clos/Alloy back up). Use **colocated** not deprecated ec2-network-lab or Clabbernetes on laptops.
- **Do not** port Clabbernetes/EKS networking hacks into the local lab.
- **Agent executes fixes** — run `make softflowd`, `make traffic`, `make stabilize`, PromQL checks yourself (WSL/bash); do not delegate shell steps to the user.
- **Hostname tagging:** `make generate` → `compose-host.generated.env` (`KTRANS_HOST`); suffixes `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` (e.g. `ktranslate-flow-<host>`). After any `ktranslate_flow` recreate, **softflowd must be repointed** (`make softflowd` — also runs at end of `make ktranslate-dev-recreate`).
- **Local collectors:** ktranslate (SNMP + NetFlow + syslog), **gnmic** (incl. LLDP neighbors) → Alloy → Grafana Cloud. Optional **topology_exporter** (`LAB_TOPOLOGY_EXPORTER=1`). Optional **Alloy-native SNMP** (`LAB_ALLOY_SNMP=1`, image `srl-local/alloy:network-dev`) runs **in parallel** by default. Colocated cutover: `LAB_KTRANSLATE=0` + `make -C local alloy-cutover-colocated` scales ktranslate to 0, enrolls Alloy remotecfg, and moves SNMP/traps/syslog/netflow River to one Fleet pipeline (`network_o11y_alloy`; CIDRs/auth names only — `snmp_config` / `config_file` / `mib_paths` default to the image library; credentials are collector `SNMP_AUTHS` / `auths_file`, not Fleet text; local ConfigMap keeps OTLP bootstrap). Optional trap cutover: `LAB_ALLOY_SNMPTRAP=1` → Alloy `loki.source.snmptrap` `:1620`. Optional syslog cutover: `LAB_ALLOY_SYSLOG=1` → Alloy `loki.source.syslog` `:1514`. Both stamp `device_name` from `snmp-targets.yml`. Optional Alloy-native flow: `LAB_ALLOY_NETFLOW=1` → `otelcol.receiver.netflow` `:2055` / sFlow `:6344` (not ktranslate `:9995`/`:6343`). Flow stamps `device_name` from `device-join.yml` (`flow.sampler_address`) and `src_host`/`dst_host` via the syslog-style LRU reverse-DNS cache (`udp_host_cache_size`; catalog name on PTR miss). Metrics default via `otelcol.connector.signaltometrics` (`network.io.by_flow`, `integration=alloy-netflow`, PromQL **`rate()`**). Logs opt-in: `LAB_ALLOY_NETFLOW_LOGS=1`. Needs `ALLOY_NETWORK_FROM_SOURCE=1`. Laptop light path: `make alloy-snmp-min` (1× SRL, no traffic/ktranslate). Discovery is Prometheus-shaped (named `auth` + SuperQ fingerprinters → hot=alerting/60s octets+oper, cold=names+packet counters+errors+discards+IP inventory, topology=optional LLDP; BGP flaps are traps/syslog) — [`docs/alloy-network-fork.md`](docs/alloy-network-fork.md). Topology SNMP scrape is opt-in (`LAB_ALLOY_SNMP_TOPOLOGY=1`). Kentik→snmp_exporter profile convert is a **one-shot ingest** (edit `snmp/modules/` after that). `fingerprinters.yml` and `snmp-network.yml` are one catalog (same convert / same image); unknown `module=` names walk empty or can panic — do not mix image YAML with older lab fixtures. Keep `table.1.column` OIDs; **full** MIB INDEX required (incomplete indexes → duplicate-label scrape failures). Converter emits curated `snmp_*` names (`snmp_CPU`, `snmp_ifHCInOctets`) — not a `kentik_snmp_*` contract. **`make up` / `make stabilize` run `post-telemetry-config.sh`** (softflowd, sFlow, syslog, traps, lab DNS, traffic, events-loop). Lab default ktranslate path: Mesverrum/KtransToGrafana.
- **Local metrics:** `kentik_snmp_*` (per-metric names — **not** `kentik_snmp_DeviceMetrics`), Alloy SNMP path `snmp_*` (`snmp_CPU` = utilization %; Unix load averages that kentik tagged CPU emit `snmp_CPULoad`; `snmp_ifHCInOctets`; `job="alloy-snmp"`; **`snmp_group`** = discovery job: `hq` laptop, `hq`/`branch1`/`branch2` colocated). Composite recording rules use Prometheus colon names (`device:snmp_MemoryUtilization:percent`, `if:snmp_ifInErrorPercent:percent`) via `make -C local alloy-snmp-recording-rules` — not converter output. Also `network_io_by_flow_bytes`, `gnmi_*` / `service_name="gnmic"`, `network_topology_device_info` / `network_topology_edge_info` (`tester_id` from `LAB_TESTER_ID`, default `network-lab`), `srl_mgmt_api_capability_info` (live + **mock** for NETCONF/JSON-RPC/gNOI/gRIBI — `local/fixtures/`, `make -C local mgmt-api-mock`) — not AWS `integrations/snmp` dashboards as-is.
- **SNMP/flow investigations:** start with `make -C local snmp-check` and `make -C local finish-flows` — full decision tree in `AGENTS.md` → *Investigation playbook*. **No flows after ktranslate recreate:** softflowd `-n` IP ≠ `ktranslate_flow` clab IP → agent runs `make softflowd` + `make traffic`. EVPN ICMP ping can fail while UDP flows work. After clab IP drift: `make snmp-recover`.
- **PromQL traps:** SNMP → `count by (device_name) (kentik_snmp_CPU)`; ktranslate flows → `count(network_io_by_flow_bytes)` and `sum(...) * 8 / 60` (no `rate()` on ktranslate rollups); Alloy-native flow is `alloy_network_io_by_flow_bytes{integration="alloy-netflow"}` (cumulative Sum — use **`rate()`** / **`increase()`**); interface bps → `(kentik_snmp_ifHCInOctets) * 8 / 60`.
- **OTLP sink:** operator's Grafana Cloud stack (`GC_OTLP_*` in `local/.env`). Optional dual-ship: `GC_OTLP_*_2` → Alloy fans out (`make generate` → `alloy/otlp-export.generated.alloy`). Helper: `local/scripts/retarget-otlp-gc.py`. Grafana Cloud MCP may be on a **different** stack than the lab — verify against `.env`.
- **Clos join app:** `make -C local join-app` — OTel HTTP on client1→client2 EVPN; Tempo `clos-join-demo` joins softflowd on port 8080; `clos_join_entity_info` / `clos_join_edge_info` overlay service+hosts on the subway nodeGraph. Talk-track latency: `make join-fault` / `join-fault-stop` (tc netem on client eth1). Identity tabs: `entity_demo_*` + dashboard `demo_model` variable (hostname / poison / mac_alias / address / iface).
- **Secrets:** never commit `local/.env`, `local/groups/*.env`, `local/state/`, or Grafana/AWS credential files.
- **Working tree:** keep this repo in sync with git. Commit harness/docs/scripts/fixtures when they change; do not leave in-flight lab work uncommitted. After an Alloy image convert, restore `../alloy/snmp/` to HEAD (do not commit convert-regenerated `snmp/modules`). Scratch `_*.sh` / `tmp-*` stay gitignored.
- **WSL2 (Windows):** clone on WSL ext4 only (`~/projects/...`); never `/mnt/c`. Use `wsl -e bash -lc` from Cursor or `.\oneclick\deploy.ps1`. Strip CRLF on new `.sh` before running (`set: pipefail\r`). Sync `scripts/` + `configs/fabric/` to WSL clone after Windows edits. **Quoting:** see `.cursor/rules/windows-shell-quoting.mdc` — write scripts to disk; never embed `$var`/heredocs in PowerShell→`wsl` strings.
- **Container exit 143:** SIGTERM (not OOM). Audit: `make -C local lab-log-status`. Never `clab deploy --reconfigure` unless user asks.
- **NetBox Cloud (optional):** `make -C local netbox-sync` when `DISCOVERY_SOURCE=netbox` in `groups/srl-hq.env` — default sample uses CIDR discovery.
- **Memory:** read and update root `AGENTS.md` (+ these rules) when architecture or bring-up changes.
- **New teammate + AI agent:** start at `AGENTS.md` → **Agent playbook** + **Investigation playbook**; then `local/README.md`. Do not assume any default Grafana Cloud stack.
- **Open work:** AWS/colocated SM private probe never came online — see `.cursor/rules/open-aws-synthetic-probe.mdc` (surface this at session start unless user asks otherwise).
- **Grafana dashboard patches (tabbed v2):** edit in **KtransToGrafana** `dashboards/`; push with `make -C local dash-push`; drift check `make -C local dash-live-sync`. **Portable skills:** `docs/grafana-network-dashboard-design-patterns.md`, `docs/grafana-network-dashboard-expand-hardware.md`. PromQL: `local/docs/dashboard-query-lessons.md`. Playbook: `docs/grafana-dashboard-playbook.md`.
